One more thing: I want to give the agents emotions — should we design the emotion/affection system first? An easily agitated agent is like it's been pumped full of adrenaline: it doesn't know to run away, it just chases you and keeps attacking. Others are rational and will dodge. And for affection: if a companion has an emotional bond with you, it's more willing to sacrifice itself. A boss might also hold a grudge against you and come at you relentlessly.
